.md
## Hough transform-like approach
Hough Transform is a popular line detection algorithm that works by mapping points in an image to lines. Why lines? The most documents are rectangular shaped, or have some tables inside or rows or columns. This is what `ImageLines` does, partially...

However, if you try to run `ImageLines` on a raw picture, you will probably generate a very large number of features. Therefore, we firstly smear out text, other small details and then find lines on already `EdgeDetect`-ed image. In this way we are no longer is looking for a global extrema

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Hough transform-like approach
Hough Transform is a popular line detection algorithm that works by mapping points in an image to lines. Why lines? The most documents are rectangular shaped, or have some tables inside or rows or columns. This is what `ImageLines` does, partially...

However, if you try to run `ImageLines` on a raw picture, you will probably generate a very large number of features. Therefore, we firstly smear out text, other small details and then find lines on already `EdgeDetect`-ed image. In this way we are no longer is looking for a global extrema

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
GaussianFilter[ColorConvert[img, "Grayscale"], 4];
HighlightImage[img, {Yellow, lines = ImageLines[EdgeDetect[%]]}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
